/**
 * The Gamma-Exponential conjugate model for latency and cost.
 *
 * A latency or cost observation `x > 0` is modeled as `x ~ Exponential(lambda)`. The rate `lambda`
 * carries a Gamma(shape, rate) posterior; the conjugate update adds one to `shape` and the observed
 * value to `rate`, so inference is closed form and online. The quantity a router cares about is the
 * expected value of the Exponential, the mean latency or mean cost, which is `1 / lambda`. Its
 * posterior is Inverse-Gamma(shape, rate) with mean `rate / (shape - 1)` for `shape > 1`. Thompson
 * sampling draws `lambda` from the Gamma posterior and returns `1 / lambda`. Nothing here approximates;
 * the credible interval is the exact Gamma quantile.
 *
 * @packageDocumentation
 */

